        "title": "Retaining Structures: Earth Pressure, Wall Types, MSE, Seismic",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Retaining structures hold back a mass of soil (or other material) against gravity and lateral loads. The driving force is lateral earth pressure from the retained soil. The resisting mechanism depends on the wall type: gravity (self-weight), cantilever (structural moment), or reinforced mass (internal reinforcement + friction)."
